# tests/abi/sco_api-v1.1.golden: the frozen ABI surface of include/sco_api.h, version 1.1.
#
# Generated by tools/abi_snapshot.py from a compiled probe (sizeof / _Alignof / offsetof /
# enum values / macros), never by reading the header as text: sco_api.h carries comments that
# have changed since sdk-v1.1.0 (its licence note), so its bytes are not the pin. What is pinned
# byte for byte is the released header itself: `git show sdk-v1.1.0:include/sco_api.h` hashes to
# the sha256 on the next line, and tools/abi_snapshot.py check verifies that hash on every run.
#
# Every line below is `<kind> <item> <value>`: sizeof, alignof, offset <struct>.<field>,
# enum <CONST>, macro <NAME>, and `fn <n> <field>` for the sco_api function pointer order (a
# reorder that leaves offsets alone still shows up there).
#
# Updating this file is deliberate, never automatic: tools/abi_snapshot.py has no mode that
# writes it. A 1.x addition (new field or function at the end of a struct, new enum value after
# the last, SCO_API_MINOR +1) gets its new lines hand-added here in the same PR as the header
# change, with the reason in the PR body. Any other difference is a break of the released ABI.
#
# Checked by: tools/test.sh, CTest `abi_freeze` (CMakeLists.txt), both on Linux, macOS and
# Windows (kernel-only builds included).
